    <title>Self-Correcting Code Agents via Execution-Grounded
  Reinforcement Learning</title>
    <summary>  Large language model agents that write code still struggle to recover from
their own mistakes. We introduce EGRL, an execution-grounded reinforcement
learning recipe that trains agents on their own repair traces, improving
SWE-bench Verified resolution rates by 11 points without inference overhead.
</summary>
    <author><name>Wei Zhang</name></author>
    <author><name>Priya Natarajan</name></author>
